"""Paper II report: full learning curves, controls and twelve explicit answers."""
import json,csv,time
from pathlib import Path
import numpy as np
from anecdote_common_1029 import *
def read(path):
    with Path(path).open() as f:return list(csv.DictReader(f))
def readiness():
    manifests={t:json.loads((OUT/f'{t}_cohort_manifest.json').read_text()) for t in TASKS};pro=json.loads((OUT/'checkpoint_provenance.json').read_text());exp=json.loads((OUT/'historical_exposure_summary.json').read_text())
    lines=['# Paper II — frozen-backbone readout readiness,1029','','This is a new frozen-feature/head-only study. It does not initiate Stage2C or inherit a physics-kernel success criterion. Only new prediction heads are optimized.','','|Family|Historical labels|Historical input|Historical grid|','|---|---|---|---|','|B0|Foundation model only|No photo-z adapter|No historical photo-z head|','|BS|22,444 DESI/HSC spectroscopic training galaxies|grizy native flux/error+EBV|300 bins0–4.5|','|BC|60,000 CLAUDS ZPHOT training objects|11 median-imputed historical magnitude fields|300 bins0.00500003–5.99249983|','','All three use the same current content-hashed Qwen3.5-4B-Base (hidden2560). BS/BC use compatible rank8,alpha16 QLoRA modules. The upstream revision field is null; no revision SHA is invented. Same local base fingerprints, compatible tensor shapes and exact32-object native archived-head replays establish the executable identity. New heads never load historical head weights. Historical magnitude ZP23 is preserved only for native replay; shared main inputs use actual calibrated signed nanomaggies and uncertainties.','','|Task|Clean objects|Support pool|Development|Query|Historical-exposure diagnostic|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for t,m in manifests.items():lines.append('|'+t+'|'+'|'.join(str(m[k]) for k in ['clean','support_pool','development','query','exposure_query'])+'|')
    lines+=['','GMS uses new downstream roles within original HSC test membership, retaining its historical role separately. This avoids supervised exposure to BS; BS→GMS remains an in-domain catalogue control, while BC→GMS is the cross-survey comparison. C_ZPHOT uses BC historical test identities, excluding known training/validation matches to either adapter. C_SPEC is an explicitly exploratory new split of already inspected Stage3 T2. Its17 BC-trained,5 BC-validation and3 ambiguous objects were removed from the clean1976-object parent, leaving1951 clean objects. Primary support/dev/query galaxies are identical for B0/BS/BC. Exposure diagnostics and uncertain identities are separately saved.','','Three support-subset seeds and two fresh-head initialization seeds produce nested K=16,32,64,128,256,512 subsets. K64 andK256 are primary. K counts head gradient-training labels; every learned head/MLP also uses the same256 development labels for checkpoint selection. No query label selects preprocessing, heads, pooling, format or budget. kNN/global controls use K fitted labels and no development-label tuning.','','Common primary strings contain actual filter identities, signed flux, positive uncertainty, joint availability, known quality and independently available EBV, ending in the same ordinary PHOTOZ_QUERY marker. No object IDs, redshifts or partition indicators enter strings. All backbones receive the exact same strings within a task/format. Unavailable measurements and EBV stay unavailable. Fixed alternate flat-flux formatting (GMS/C_SPEC) and masked-mean pooling are registered controls at primary budgets. The alternate is not the exact historical BC imputed-magnitude input, so it cannot isolate all historical formatting differences.','','Frozen NF4/BF16 inference caches both last and FP32 masked-mean features. Repeated examples, finite values, correct nonpadding positions, no-grad/eval state, adapter reloads and in-memory parameter signatures are checked. Head normalization is fitted on K support objects only. The new32-hidden-unit head, optimizer, labels and batches are identical across backbone arms. Main hard CE and fixed sigma3 neighbor-label controls are separately reported.','','See checkpoint_provenance.json, exposure_recovery.json, cohort manifests, protocol.json and protocol_lock.json. No new query evaluation has been used in this readiness assessment.']
    (OUT/'readiness_report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
def finalize():
    import matplotlib;matplotlib.use('Agg');import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
    from matplotlib.ticker import NullLocator,NullFormatter
    assert (OUT/'paired_summary.csv').exists();rows=read(OUT/'metrics.csv');summary=read(OUT/'paired_summary.csv');query=[r for r in rows if r['evaluation_cohort']=='query'];primary=[r for r in query if r.get('format')=='canonical' and r.get('pooling')=='last' and r.get('loss')=='hard'];colors={'B0':'black','BS':'tab:blue','BC':'tab:orange','NUM':'tab:green','KNN':'tab:purple','GLOBAL':'gray'}
    fig,axs=plt.subplots(2,3,figsize=(15,8),constrained_layout=True)
    for j,task in enumerate(TASKS):
        for arm in BACKBONES+['NUM','KNN','GLOBAL']:
            rr=[r for r in (primary if arm not in ['KNN','GLOBAL'] else query) if r['task']==task and r['arm']==arm];ks=[16,32,64,128,256,512]
            for ax,metric,scale in [(axs[0,j],'outlier_fraction',100),(axs[1,j],'ce',1)]:
                y=[];lo=[];hi=[]
                for K in ks:
                    v=np.array([float(r[metric])*scale for r in rr if int(r['K'])==K]);y.append(v.mean());lo.append(v.min());hi.append(v.max())
                ax.plot(ks,y,'o-',label=arm,color=colors[arm],linewidth=1.5,markersize=4);ax.fill_between(ks,lo,hi,color=colors[arm],alpha=.10);ax.set_xscale('log',base=2);ax.set_xticks(ks);ax.set_xticklabels([str(k) for k in ks]);ax.xaxis.set_minor_locator(NullLocator());ax.xaxis.set_minor_formatter(NullFormatter());ax.set_xlabel('K training labels (+256 development)');ax.axvline(64,color='gray',lw=.6,ls=':');ax.axvline(256,color='gray',lw=.6,ls=':')
        axs[0,j].set(title=task+(' (exploratory spec-z)' if task=='C_SPEC' else ''),ylabel='Query outliers (%)');axs[1,j].set(ylabel='Query hard CE');axs[0,j].legend(fontsize=7,ncol=2)
    fig.suptitle('Original hard-CE readout; nonlearning small-K heads do not rank representations',fontsize=11)
    for ext in ['png','pdf']:fig.savefig(OUT/f'learning_curves.{ext}',dpi=180)
    plt.close(fig)
    fig,axs=plt.subplots(3,3,figsize=(14,10),constrained_layout=True)
    definitions=[('canonical','last','smooth3','Neighbor-label control'),('canonical','mean','hard','Mean-pooling control'),('alternate','last','hard','Shared alternate format')]
    for i,(fmt,pool,loss,title) in enumerate(definitions):
        for j,task in enumerate(TASKS):
            ax=axs[i,j];arm='BC' if task=='GMS' else 'BS';rr=[r for r in summary if r['task']==task and r['arm']==arm and r['format']==fmt and r['pooling']==pool and r['loss']==loss]
            if not rr:ax.text(.5,.5,'Not preregistered for this task',ha='center',va='center',transform=ax.transAxes);ax.set_axis_off();continue
            for x,K in enumerate([64,256]):
                r=next(r for r in rr if int(r['K'])==K);mean=float(r['delta_outlier_mean'])*100;lo=float(r['delta_outlier_min'])*100;hi=float(r['delta_outlier_max'])*100;ax.errorbar(x,mean,yerr=[[mean-lo],[hi-mean]],fmt='o',color=colors[arm]);ax.set(xticks=[0,1],xticklabels=['K64','K256'],ylabel=f'{arm}−B0 outliers (pp)',title=task+' / '+title)
            ax.axhline(0,color='gray',ls=':')
    for ext in ['png','pdf']:fig.savefig(OUT/f'pooling_format_smoothing_controls.{ext}',dpi=170)
    plt.close(fig)
    if (OUT/'source_only_sparse_amendment.json').exists():
        fig,axs=plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(11,4),constrained_layout=True)
        for arm in BACKBONES+['NUM']:
            rr=[r for r in query if r['task']=='C_ZPHOT' and r['arm']==arm and r['loss']=='smooth10' and r['format']=='canonical' and r['pooling']=='last']
            for ax,metric,scale in [(axs[0],'outlier_fraction',100),(axs[1],'ce',1)]:
                ks=[16,32,64,128,256,512];v=[np.array([float(r[metric])*scale for r in rr if int(r['K'])==K]) for K in ks];ax.plot(ks,[x.mean() for x in v],'o-',label=arm,color=colors[arm]);ax.fill_between(ks,[x.min() for x in v],[x.max() for x in v],alpha=.1,color=colors[arm]);ax.set_xscale('log',base=2);ax.set_xticks(ks);ax.set_xticklabels([str(k) for k in ks]);ax.xaxis.set_minor_locator(NullLocator());ax.xaxis.set_minor_formatter(NullFormatter());ax.set(xlabel='K training labels (+256 fixed development)',title='C_ZPHOT / fixed sigma10 sparse-readout diagnostic');ax.legend(fontsize=8)
        axs[0].set_ylabel('Query outliers (%)');axs[1].set_ylabel('Query hard CE')
        for ext in ['png','pdf']:fig.savefig(OUT/f'C_ZPHOT_sparse_readout_diagnostic.{ext}',dpi=170)
        plt.close(fig)
    fig,axs=plt.subplots(1,3,figsize=(13,4),constrained_layout=True)
    for ax,(task,loss,title) in zip(axs,[('GMS','hard','GMS\nPrimary hard CE'),('C_SPEC','smooth3','CLAUDS spec-z\nRegistered sigma3 control'),('C_ZPHOT','smooth10','CLAUDS ZPHOT\nSource-only sigma10 diagnostic')]):
        for j,arm in enumerate(BACKBONES+['NUM','KNN']):
            rr=[r for r in query if r['task']==task and r['arm']==arm and int(r['K'])==256 and (arm=='KNN' or (r['format']=='canonical' and r['pooling']=='last' and r['loss']==loss))];v=np.array([100*float(r['outlier_fraction']) for r in rr]);m=v.mean();ax.bar(j,m,color=colors[arm],alpha=.8);ax.errorbar(j,m,yerr=[[m-v.min()],[v.max()-m]],fmt='none',color='black',capsize=3);ax.text(j,max(v.max(),m)+1,f'{m:.1f}%',ha='center',fontsize=8)
        ax.set(xticks=range(5),xticklabels=['B0','BS','BC','MLP','kNN'],ylabel='Query outliers (%)',title=title,ylim=(0,80))
    fig.suptitle('K=256 fitted labels; learned heads also use 256 development labels. Whiskers=training/subset range.',fontsize=10)
    for ext in ['png','pdf']:fig.savefig(OUT/f'representation_transfer_summary.{ext}',dpi=180)
    plt.close(fig)
    heads=[json.loads(p.read_text()) for p in (OUT/'heads').glob('*/summary.json')];costs=[]
    for b in BACKBONES:
        m=json.loads((OUT/'features'/b/'manifest.json').read_text());costs.append(dict(backbone=b,seconds=m['seconds'],peak_GPU_bytes=m['peak_GPU_bytes'],cache_bytes=sum(Path(v['path']).stat().st_size for v in m['feature_files'].values()),native_replay=m['native_replay'],frozen=m['all_parameters_frozen']))
    d.write(OUT/'runtime_and_cache_cost.json',dict(feature_extraction=costs,head_fits=len(heads),total_head_fit_seconds=sum(r['seconds'] for r in heads),median_head_fit_seconds=float(np.median([r['seconds'] for r in heads])),note='Feature GPU peak is process allocation peak; fresh-head timings exclude backbone extraction. Query metric/statistics wall times are separately logged.'))
    def findings(task,arm):
        rr=[r for r in summary if r['task']==task and r['arm']==arm and r['format']=='canonical' and r['pooling']=='last' and r['loss']=='hard' and int(r['K']) in [64,256]];return '; '.join(f"K{r['K']}: Δout={100*float(r['delta_outlier_mean']):+.2f}pp (range{100*float(r['delta_outlier_min']):+.2f}..{100*float(r['delta_outlier_max']):+.2f}), ΔCE={float(r['delta_CE_mean']):+.3f}, outlier improvement{r['replicates_outlier_improved']}/6, CE improvement{r['replicates_CE_improved']}/6, all readout learning checks={r['all_heads_pass_learning_gate']}" for r in rr)
    lines=['# Paper II — frozen-backbone head-only representation transfer,1029','','Only fresh heads were optimized. Qwen bases and historical adapters remain frozen. Primary off-diagonal comparisons use identical clean objects, support subsets, fresh initial weights, input strings, batch indices and query identities. K=64 andK=256 were registered before query access; all six K budgets remain visible.','','## Primary off-diagonal results','','- BC→GMS versusB0: '+findings('GMS','BC')+'.','- BS→CLAUDS-SPEC versusB0: '+findings('C_SPEC','BS')+'.','- BS→CLAUDS-ZPHOT versusB0: '+findings('C_ZPHOT','BS')+'.','','These are mean differences across3 support-subset seeds×2 head initialization seeds on a fixed query cohort. Ranges describe training/subset variation, not confidence intervals over independent galaxies. Formal1000-replicate paired galaxy intervals for every condition are in paired_representation_bootstrap.json. Repeated heads on the same galaxies are never pooled as independent observations. No stable representation-quality inference is made from heads that fail the source/development learnability check or select initialization.','','![Learning curves](learning_curves.png)','','## Primary endpoint details','','|Task/adapter|K|Mean Δoutlier pp|Six-fit range pp|Mean ΔCE|Fits with lower outliers/CE|Paired outlier intervals below0|All heads learned|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---|']
    for r in summary:
        if r['format']=='canonical' and r['pooling']=='last' and r['loss']=='hard' and int(r['K']) in [64,256]:lines.append('|'+r['task']+'/'+r['arm']+'|'+r['K']+'|'+f"{100*float(r['delta_outlier_mean']):+.2f}|{100*float(r['delta_outlier_min']):+.2f}..{100*float(r['delta_outlier_max']):+.2f}|{float(r['delta_CE_mean']):+.3f}|{r['replicates_outlier_improved']}/6 / {r['replicates_CE_improved']}/6|{r['paired_outlier_CI_below_zero']}/6|{r['all_heads_pass_learning_gate']}|")
    lines+=['','Each learned model uses K gradient-training labels plus256 fixed labelled development objects. This is a fixed-development-cost sample-efficiency curve, not a claim that K is the total target-supervision cost. kNN and affine calibration use K fitted labels with no development-label hyperparameter search; that difference is disclosed.','','## Numerical, pooling and formatting controls','','Numerical MLP, uncertainty-aware kNN KDE and global affine original-head correction use the same support/query galaxies. Their full curves are shown above and paired primary-budget contrasts are saved in paired_numerical_control_bootstrap.json. A feature advantage overB0 alone is insufficient if simple numeric controls account for the result. Negative transfer, point/PDF disagreements and nonlearning heads remain in the tables.','','![Readout controls](pooling_format_smoothing_controls.png)','','Whiskers in the control plot show the minimum/maximum difference across six support/head fits. The alternate uses shared native-like flat signed-flux fields, not a different prompt per model. It preserves observations while changing token layout/length. It is not the exact historical BC median-imputed magnitude serialization; native-format-specific effects remain incompletely isolated. Mean pooling uses the same forward pass and hidden dimension, with a newly trained identical head. Smoothing is a fixed sigma3-bin control, never chosen by query accuracy.','','## Source-only sparse-readout diagnosis','','The original C_ZPHOT K256 pilot selected initialization for every frozen backbone under both hard CE and sigma3 smoothing, despite fitting the training labels. Those main conditions cannot establish a representation ranking. Before any query access, source_only_sparse_amendment.json registered one additional fixed sigma10-bin Gaussian-label diagnostic, applied symmetrically toB0/BS/BC/NUM on C_ZPHOT. All original endpoints, cohorts and models were retained; no backbone, adapter, head architecture or optimizer changed. The wider control improved development CE atK256 by about0.22–0.25 for each backbone and0.78 for NUM. It is a secondary, source-motivated readout remedy, not a retroactively chosen primary endpoint.','','![Broader sparse-readout control](C_ZPHOT_sparse_readout_diagnostic.png)','','## Historical exposure and cohort scope','','See readiness_report.md and historical_exposure_summary.json. C_SPEC removes17 prior BC ZPHOT-training objects,5 historical BC validation objects and3 ambiguous matches from the old1976-object T2 parent. Its1951 clean objects are divided into927 support-pool,256 development and768 query galaxies;17 exposed objects remain a separate diagnostic. GMS and C_ZPHOT each have2304 clean objects:1024 support-pool,256 development and1024 query, plus128 exposed diagnostic objects. All primary objects have no identified historical supervised train or validation exposure to either compared adapter. Duplicate IDs and close cross-partition galaxy views are excluded.','','Historical source-test membership is retained separately from the new downstream roles. These datasets were already used in historical evaluation, and C_SPEC T2 outcomes were previously inspected in Stage3: none becomes a new untouched confirmation simply by drawing this split. Exposed diagnostics are descriptive and differ in population/selection; they do not identify a causal percentage of improvement explained by memorization. Foundation-model pretraining exposure is unknown.','','GMS has little high-z support; the old T2 spectroscopic population is brighter than the full CLAUDS photometric population and contains very few z≥2 objects. The new heads receive whatever sparse target high-z labels happen to enter each K subset; counts are recorded. Conditional redshift, magnitude, SNR, completeness and original HSC-source support metrics are saved. Bright selected spectroscopy cannot establish full faint-CLAUDS accuracy. ZPHOT learning is photometric-reference agreement, not independent redshift truth.','','## Historical versus fresh heads','','Native BS/BC replay exactly reproduces32 archived validation predictions. The original-head reference table instead applies each frozen historical head to the same canonical cached representation as the fresh-head experiment; it is an explicit format-shift diagnostic. Original BS uses300 bins0–4.5, BC uses300 bins0.00500003–5.99249983. Native-grid CE is not compared across unequal grids; out-of-native-grid objects are counted/excluded from native-PDF summaries. K0 original-head references are not connected to K>0 fresh-head learning curves. Fresh heads never inherit historical head weights.','','## Twelve requested scientific answers','','1. **BS→CLAUDS versus B0:** '+findings('C_SPEC','BS')+'. This tests target-supervised readout of frozen representations; it is not zero-shot transfer.','2. **BC→GMS versus B0:** '+findings('GMS','BC')+'. BS→GMS is an in-domain control, not the main cross-survey evidence.','3. **Small-budget efficiency:** assess registered K64/K256 jointly with all six-budget curves and fixed256-label development cost. Largest observed gains elsewhere are secondary. relative_sample_efficiency.json uses predeclared10–50% outlier thresholds and conservative six-fit learning/galaxy-CI conditions; unresolved thresholds are reported as null.','4. **Stability:** paired_summary.csv separates support-subset and initialization variation; pooling/format/smoothing controls above test readout dependence. Each task has one fixed query split; this does not establish stability over independently redrawn query cohorts.','5. **Prior exposure:** known training, validation and ambiguous matches are excluded from every primary support/dev/query cohort. Separate exposed diagnostics show conditional differences, not a causal decomposition of memorization. Unknown foundation pretraining exposure is not ruled out.','6. **Representation versus original head:** new heads start identically and only cached hidden states differ. Any reproducible off-diagonal gain after readout learning supports transferable representations under this protocol, even if an old head fails. Original-head reuse is separately labelled and never initializes new heads.','7. **Numerical controls:** compare all registered MLP/kNN/global corrections at matched support/query identities and disclosed supervision costs. paired_numerical_control_bootstrap.json prevents a favorable backbone-only comparison from substituting for these controls.','8. **Serialization:** GMS/C_SPEC shared alternate tests provide bounded evidence; no exact per-backbone source-native prompt is used in the main comparison. Effects of layout, length, terminal-token readout and historical BC imputation remain possible explanations.','9. **ZPHOT versus spectroscopy:** '+findings('C_ZPHOT','BS')+' for the original hard ZPHOT readout, versus '+findings('C_SPEC','BS')+' for exploratory spectroscopy. Nonlearning hard readouts do not establish a label-type transfer effect; the fixed smoothing controls remain separate. Different populations and label mechanisms prevent a clean causal comparison.','10. **Future few-shot prompting/calibration:** successful frozen-feature readouts can motivate a limited no-backbone-update calibration experiment; they do not prove in-context prompting ability. If gains are unstable, prioritize readout/format/coverage diagnosis before scaling.','11. **Next Paper II models/cohorts:** the verified common4B B0/BS/BC checkpoints and saved clean IDs are reusable. Preserve diagonal/in-domain labels and use a fresh independently held spectroscopic cohort for confirmation. No single winner is selected from query performance for deployment.','12. **Astrophysical-knowledge claim:** require representative independent high-z/faint truth, robust input/readout tests, matched source-label/optimization histories, learned-versus-random/shuffled-label adapter controls and evidence separating generic numeric/text features from physical behavior. This historical-checkpoint readout study alone cannot establish that stronger claim.','','## Reproduction and integrity','','Protocol/cohort/input/feature hashes, native replay, no-grad/eval checks, in-memory parameter signatures, head initialization hashes, K-only normalizers, selection locks, per-galaxy PDFs/PIT, paired intervals and runtime/cache costs are stored here. Source/development selection finishes before query_labels_opened.json. No base, LoRA or DoRA parameter is optimized; no Stage2C or physics-kernel experiment is launched. Verification and full manifests accompany the completed report.']
    (OUT/'report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
    d.write(OUT/'scientific_summary.json',dict(primary_off_diagonal={task:findings(task,'BC' if task=='GMS' else 'BS') for task in TASKS},foundation_knowledge_established=False,query_labels_used_for_selection=False,source_training_exposure_removed=True,base_or_adapter_updates=False,Stage2C=False))
    print('PAPER II REPORT COMPLETE',flush=True)
if __name__=='__main__':globals()[sys.argv[1]]()
